A render pass that clears its colour attachment on load: VulkanFramebuffer::renderPassClearColor (the same
attachments, the colour load op CLEAR, the depth-stencil ones as in renderPass) and renderPassClearColorDepth (both
CLEAR, as renderPassClearDepth), compatible with renderPass, and VulkanCommandList::pendingColorClear, used by the
next render pass the command list begins (to zero; with pendingDepthClear, both) and forgotten by setFramebuffer.
A pass whose first draw writes every pixel of its render area begins with it: a tile-based GPU then neither reads
the old colour nor clears it with a draw. (A CLEAR, not DONT_CARE: the MHGU port saw an Adreno 830 draw a scene
black but for some tiles after DONT_CARE.)

